RESOLUTION NO. 2026-45
A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF LAKE ELSINORE,
CALIFORNIA, CALLING FOR THE HOLDING OF A GENERAL MUNICIPAL
ELECTION TO BE HELD ON NOVEMBER 3, 2026, FOR THE ELECTION OF
CITY COUNCIL MEMBERS IN DISTRICT 1 (FULL FOUR‑YEAR TERM),
DISTRICT 3 (FULL FOUR‑YEAR TERM), AND DISTRICT 4 (TWO‑YEAR
UNEXPIRED BALANCE OF TERM FORMERLY HELD BY COUNCIL MEMBER
NATASHA JOHNSON) AS REQUIRED BY THE PROVISIONS OF THE LAWS
OF THE STATE OF CALIFORNIA RELATING TO GENERAL LAW CITIES AND
FOR THE SUBMISSION TO THE VOTERS A QUESTION RELATING TO
WHETHER THE OFFICE OF CITY TREASURER SHALL BE CHANGED FROM
AN ELECTED OFFICE TO AN APPOINTED OFFICE, AND SETTING RELATED
PROCEDURES
Whereas, under the provisions of the laws relating to general law cities in the State of
California, a General Municipal Election shall be held on November 3, 2026, for the election of
Municipal Officers; and
Whereas, the City Council also desires to submit to the voters at the election a question
relating to whether the office of the City Treasurer shall be changed from an Elected office to an
Appointed office.
NOW, THEREFORE, THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF LAKE ELSINORE DOES
HEREBY RESOLVE, DETERMINE, AND ORDER AS FOLLOWS:
Section 1. That pursuant to the requirements of the laws of the State of California
relating to General Law Cities, there is called and ordered to be held in the City of Lake Elsinore,
California, on Tuesday, November 3, 2026, a General Municipal Election for the purpose of
electing two Members of the City Council (Districts 1 and 3) for a full term of four years and one
Member of the City Council (District 4) for a partial term of two years.
Section 2. That the City Council, pursuant to its right and authority, does order
submitted to the voters at the General Municipal Election the following question:
Shall the office of City Treasurer be appointive?
YES
NO
Section 3. That the proposed complete text of the measure submitted to the voters is
attached as Exhibit A.
Section 4. That the vote requirement for the measure to pass is a majority (50%+1) of
the votes cast.
Section 5. That the ballots to be used at the election shall be in form and content as
required by law.
