ORDINANCE NO. 2026-
AN ORDINANCE OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF LAKE ELSINORE,
CALIFORNIA, AMENDING LAKE ELSINORE MUNICIPAL CODE CHAPTER
2.42 (CITY TREASURER) OF TITLE 2 (ADMINISTRATION AND PERSONNEL)
TO MAKE THE OFFICE OF CITY TREASURER AN APPOINTIVE OFFICE
Whereas, Government Code Section 36508 and Elections Code Section 9222 authorize
the City Council to submit to the electors the question of whether the elective City Treasurer shall
be an appointive office and, if a majority of voters voting on the measure approve it, the office
shall become appointive; and
Whereas, an appointive City Treasurer will be required to possess relevant experience in
government finance and a professional financial background, training, skills, and experience
necessary to fulfill the important responsibilities of the office of City Treasurer; and
Whereas, on May 12, 2026, pursuant to State law, the City Council adopted Resolution
No. 2026-XX, submitting this ordinance to the voters at the General Municipal Election on
Tuesday, November 3, 2026; and
Whereas, all other legal prerequisites to the adoption of this ordinance have occurred.
NOW THEREFORE, THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF LAKE ELSINORE DOES
ORDAIN AS FOLLOWS:
Section 1. Subject to the approval of a majority of the voters of the City of Lake Elsinore
at the scheduled election so designated by the City Council in a separate resolution placing this
proposal on the ballot for such election, Chapter 2.42 of Title 2 of the Lake Elsinore Municipal Code
is hereby amended to read as follows:
2.42.010 Office established.
As of the November 5, 2028 Municipal Election or the earlier vacancy of the elected City
Treasurer position, the office of the City Treasurer shall cease to be elected as provided
by law and shall become an appointive office. Pursuant to California Government Code
Section 36510, the City Treasurer shall be appointed by the City Manager. The City
Manager may self-appoint to serve as City Treasurer, appoint the Director of Finance, or
appoint another professional with relevant experience in government finance and a
professional financial background, training, skills, and experience necessary to serve as
City Treasurer.
2.42.020 Elective office.
The City Treasurer shall be elected from the City at large at a general municipal election.
2.42.030 Term of office.
The City Treasurer shall serve for a term of four years and until his successor is elected
and qualified.
