2.42.050 Eligibility.
No person shall be eligible to hold the office of City Treasurer unless such person, at the
time of assuming office, shall be a qualified elector of the City and shall have been a
resident of the City for at least the minimum period provided by law next preceding the
date of such person’s election or appointment.
2.42.060 Vacancies.
A vacancy in the office of City Treasurer shall be filled by appointment by the City Council.
Such appointee shall hold office until the next succeeding general municipal election and
until his successor is elected and qualified.
2.42.070 Failure to fill vacancy.
In the event that the City Council shall fail to fill a vacancy by appointment within 30 days
after such office has become vacant, the City Council shall forthwith call a special election
to fill such vacancy; provided, that if such vacancy occurs within 120 days prior to a general
municipal election, such vacancy shall be filled at the general municipal election.
2.42.080 Powers and duties.
The City Treasurer shall be the custodian of all public funds belonging to or under the
control of the City or of any office, department or agency of the City and shall perform such
duties as may be prescribed from time to time by the City Council consistent with this
chapter and applicable law.
2.42.020 Bond Requirements
Pursuant to California Government Code Section 36518, the City Treasurer shall furnish
a corporate surety bond to be approved by the City Council in the same amount as that
required of the Director of Finance and City Clerk, and it shall be conditioned upon the
satisfactory performance of the duties imposed upon the City Treasurer by statute,
ordinance, or resolution. Any premium for such bond shall be a proper charge against the
City of Lake Elsinore.
2.42.030 Powers and duties.
The City Treasurer shall perform the duties as are prescribed by California Government
Code Sections 41001 through 41007 and by any other provisions of law applicable to the
deposit, investment, and safekeeping of public funds of the City.
